### Proof architecture
Built 7 `private` helpers to run the whole `μ ⊗ signVec ⊗ gaussVec` argument in per-outcome iterated-integral style (no `Measure.prod` associativity):
- **`jensen_pointwise`** — inserts `E|g|=√(2/π)` fibrewise, `norm_integral_le_integral_norm`, kills constant with `√(π/2)·√(2/π)=1`
- **`cov_gaussVec`** — the `(εᵢ|gᵢ|)ᵢ =ᵈ (gᵢ)ᵢ` change of variables via `integral_map` + `map_signVec_mul_abs_pi`
- **`upper_inner` / `lower_inner`** — the two directions per fixed vector family (lower uses `contraction_principle` at coefficients `|gᵢ|` + `integral_pi_norm_gaussVec_le`)
- Integrability bricks: **`integrable_eval_signVec`**, **`integrable_normX`** (`Integrable.op_fst_snd`), **`integrable_abs_prod`** (`Integrable.mul_prod`), **`integrable_norm_gaussVec`**, plus **`norm_abs_pi`**

